WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.135
Step 1. Open the schedule.

1.2
00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:07.064
A schedule template lets Care make bookable slots from its sessions.

1.3
00:00:07.064 --> 00:00:13.291
Select Users, then See Details for the practitioner, then the Availability tab.

2.1
00:00:13.291 --> 00:00:18.663
Step 2. Start the template. On the Schedule tab, select Create Template.

2.2
00:00:18.663 --> 00:00:24.997
The Create Schedule Template sheet opens, with one empty session ready to fill in.

3.1
00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:30.706
Step 3. Name the template. Enter the Template Name, here Evening OP.

3.2
00:00:30.706 --> 00:00:37.548
The name is required. If you leave it empty, Care shows This field is required.

4.1
00:00:37.548 --> 00:00:39.871
Step 4. Set the valid period.

4.2
00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:44.876
Select the Valid Period field, choose the Start date and the End date,

4.3
00:00:44.876 --> 00:00:46.163
then select Apply.

4.4
00:00:46.163 --> 00:00:51.381
Care blocks the days before today, so the start date can be today.

5.1
00:00:51.381 --> 00:00:56.915
Step 5. Select the weekdays. Under Weekly Schedule, select Mon to Fri.

5.2
00:00:56.915 --> 00:01:00.840
The weekdays apply to every session in the template,

5.3
00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:03.830
and you must select at least one.

6.1
00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:09.339
Step 6. Set the visibility. Make the template public is clear by default,

6.2
00:01:09.339 --> 00:01:12.724
so patients cannot book these slots themselves.

6.3
00:01:12.724 --> 00:01:16.970
Staff see the slots of public and private templates.

7.1
00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:21.174
Step 7. Set the encounter defaults. This step is optional.

7.2
00:01:21.174 --> 00:01:26.765
Encounter defaults are applied when an encounter is created from an appointment on

7.3
00:01:26.765 --> 00:01:30.061
this schedule. Here you leave them empty.

8.1
00:01:30.061 --> 00:01:35.881
Step 8. Fill in the session. Enter the Session Title, Start Time, End Time,

8.2
00:01:35.881 --> 00:01:39.148
Slot duration (mins.) and Patients per Slot.

8.3
00:01:39.148 --> 00:01:45.812
A note then shows the number of slots and about how many minutes each patient gets.

9.1
00:01:45.812 --> 00:01:48.930
Step 11. Save the template. Select Save.

9.2
00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.515
Care shows Schedule template created successfully,

9.3
00:01:52.515 --> 00:01:58.324
and the template appears on the Schedule tab for the months that its valid period

9.4
00:01:58.324 --> 00:01:59.326
covers.
